  // A pieces editor that was just opened (or fed from the hint) takes the focus, so the keyboard carries on inside it (its box, not a
  // field: a touch screen keyboard should not pop up over the hint). When the editor closes, the focus goes back to the line's button.
  // A box taller than the lines box is scrolled into view by its top (below the sticky column header), so its title and hint stay in sight.
  useEffect(() => {
    const sel = focusTo.current;
